mmdevapi: do not re-wrap the friendly name of an absent device

The registry loop that re-creates devices which are no longer present reads
DEVPKEY_Device_FriendlyName and passes it to MMDevice_Create as the driver id.
MMDevice_Create builds the device friendly name from that id as
"Speakers (%s)" -- or "Microphone (%s)" -- and writes the result back, so each
enumeration wraps the stored name in another layer.

The growth is unbounded and persists in the registry. An unplugged monitor's
HDMI endpoint in a long-lived bottle had accumulated 97 of them:

  "Speakers (Speakers (Speakers ( ... (DELL S2817Q) ... )))"

Read DEVPKEY_DeviceInterface_FriendlyName instead. That is where the same
function stores the unwrapped driver id, so re-creating an absent device now
reproduces the name it had rather than decorating it again.

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
index 7fd518de0f6..321280e3970 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
@@ -792,9 +792,15 @@ HRESULT load_devices_from_reg(void)
         if (ret != ERROR_SUCCESS)
             continue;
         if (SUCCEEDED(CLSIDFromString(guidvalue, &guid))
-            && SUCCEEDED(MMDevice_GetPropValue(&guid, curflow, (const PROPERTYKEY*)&DEVPKEY_Device_FriendlyName, &pv))
+            && SUCCEEDED(MMDevice_GetPropValue(&guid, curflow, (const PROPERTYKEY*)&DEVPKEY_DeviceInterface_FriendlyName, &pv))
             && pv.vt == VT_LPWSTR)
         {
+            /* The interface friendly name, not the device one: MMDevice_Create
+             * takes a driver id and builds the device friendly name from it as
+             * "Speakers (%s)", then writes that back. Reading the device name
+             * here fed it its own output, so every enumeration of an absent
+             * device wrapped the stored name in another "Speakers (...)".
+             * Found 97 layers deep on an unplugged monitor's HDMI endpoint. */
             MMDevice_Create(pv.pwszVal, &guid, curflow,
                     DEVICE_STATE_NOTPRESENT, FALSE);
             CoTaskMemFree(pv.pwszVal);
